From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 23:23:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi-system-iface: honor wifi.interface in SetWifiUpState

SetWifiUpState() hardcoded "wlan0", but the wifi AIDL HAL already names its
STA interface from the wifi.interface system property (getWlanIfaceName in
wifi_chip.cpp). On a device whose interface is not wlan0, the legacy HAL's
start() brings the interface up via SetWifiUpState() before wifi_initialize,
so the SIOCGIFFLAGS on the missing wlan0 fails and the whole HAL start
fails with "Failed to set WiFi interface up".

Read wifi.interface (defaulting to wlan0) so this path matches the name the
rest of the stack uses.

Change-Id: I9601a3b85eae5354997ffa1870bc22d28b72dd8a
---
 libwifi_system_iface/interface_tool.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libwifi_system_iface/interface_tool.cpp b/libwifi_system_iface/interface_tool.cpp
index 2dc23a3..19b1666 100644
--- a/libwifi_system_iface/interface_tool.cpp
+++ b/libwifi_system_iface/interface_tool.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <linux/if.h>
 
 #include <android-base/logging.h>
+#include <android-base/properties.h>
 #include <android-base/unique_fd.h>
 
 #define IFNAMSIZ    16
@@ -109,7 +110,11 @@ bool InterfaceTool::SetUpState(const char* if_name, bool request_up) {
 }
 
 bool InterfaceTool::SetWifiUpState(bool request_up) {
-  return SetUpState(kWlan0InterfaceName, request_up);
+  // Honor the same property the wifi AIDL HAL uses to name its STA iface
+  // (see getWlanIfaceName in wifi_chip.cpp) instead of assuming wlan0.
+  std::string ifname =
+      base::GetProperty("wifi.interface", kWlan0InterfaceName);
+  return SetUpState(ifname.c_str(), request_up);
 }
 
 bool InterfaceTool::SetMacAddress(const char* if_name,
